                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The art is nice, and the soundtrack is nice, that is the only good thing about this game. The gameplay is terrible, the player can't do anything. I lost interest the moment I looked at a guide and realized, 2 hours in, that i've only completed the first couple of steps. This game leave zero clues on what the player has to do to progress through the game. Where I gave up: opened up the laboratory, got the recipe, read the note about the \"code\" relating to a \"festival\" couldn't find any number, or mentions of a festival in any of the accessible rooms, wasn't allowed to pick up any ingredient, or make any further progress. Tentacles want something sweet, can't make or find anything sweet. Plants obviously need music because of record player and records in the room, but can't do anything with them. Wolf boy wants meat, has matches, and access to kitchen, but can't do anything with any of those.",
